        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "ECDSA keypair machinery for Bitcoin: OpenSSL EC_KEY objects on secp256k1, created by the EC_KEY_new_by_curve_name_NID_secp256k1 factory (198/214/254) and consumed by Bitcoin_MakePublicKeyFromPrivateKey, which loads the 32-byte private key via BN_bin2bn, completes with EC_POINT_mul scalar multiplication (keys.c:288), sets private/public key parts, and serializes with i2o_ECPublicKey. Shor recovers the private key from the public key — funds theft, not just forgery. Not application-changeable: Bit"
